{"nodes": [{"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02901_frame", "label": "Frame 02901 - Infrared Overhead Broiler House View (Siren Camera, 2022-02-24 22:02:21)", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02901.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2022-02-24T22:02:21", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Late-evening IR frame with markedly lower apparent occupancy than the other Siren frames: birds sit in loose feeder-centred rosettes with wide empty litter between them, making individual birds cleanly separable."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02901_resting_posture_cluster", "label": "Resting / Sitting Posture Cluster", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02901.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Away from the feeders, birds appear as compact rounded blobs with no visible leg or neck extension, consistent with sitting or resting rather than walking or feeding. Posture compactness read from an overhead silhouette is the main cue available for separating resting from active behaviour in this dataset."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02901_flock_growth_progression", "label": "Flock Growth Progression Across Capture Dates", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02901.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Apparent bird size grows steadily from the 2022-02-22 frames through 2022-02-23 and 2022-02-24 to the 2022-03-01 frames, spanning roughly a week of the grow-out cycle. Object scale is therefore not stationary across the folder, so a detector with a fixed anchor scale or a fixed-radius counting kernel will degrade at one end of the date range."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02901_low_light_grayscale_domain_gap", "label": "Day/Night Domain Gap in Capture Conditions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02901.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The chunk splits into two visually incompatible domains - monochrome low-contrast IR and full-colour lit frames - captured by the same camera at different hours. This is why the test set deliberately mixes both: a model validated only on colour frames would not be shown to generalise to the IR night regime, which is exactly when much resting behaviour occurs."}], "edges": [{"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02901_frame", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02901_resting_posture_cluster", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02901.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02901_frame", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame01701_infrared_night_vision_mode", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02901.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02901_frame", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis